-   `unknown', GCC's config.sub canonicalises the same target to `none'.  */
-#define ASM_SPEC "-triple=wasm32-unknown-unknown -filetype=obj %{v:--show-encoding} %{Wa,*:%*}"
+   `unknown', GCC's config.sub canonicalises the same target to `none'.
+
+   -mattr=+atomics,+bulk-memory is what lets the atomic memory instructions be
+   assembled: llvm-mc keeps them behind the feature flag and REJECTS them without
+   it, "instruction requires: atomics".  Unlike the exception-handling proposal's
+   instructions, which the `eh_instructions' subject in
+   Tools/wasm_dialect_probe.py found are mis-type-checked rather than refused --
+   so a missing feature flag is not one failure mode here, it is two, and only
+   this one announces itself.
+
+   Thread-local storage ASSEMBLES without the flag; what it needs the features for
+   is the link, through the target_features section wasm_asm_file_end emits.
+   wasm-ld refuses TLS outright unless atomics AND bulk-memory are declared
+   ("'bulk-memory' feature must be used in order to use thread-local storage"), so
+   the two are enabled as a pair even for a unit that uses only TLS.
