+   emutls makes a `__thread' variable a control object plus a per-thread copy
+   allocated by __emutls_get_address, and that model cannot share a variable with
+   a library compiled by another compiler.  wasi-libc's errno is exactly that
+   case -- clang gives it real wasm TLS in a .tdata segment, and a GCC that asked
+   for `__emutls_v.errno' instead would want a symbol nothing defines, which is
+   where step 17 met this.  There is no emutls-to-native bridge to write; the
+   target either addresses the segment the way the rest of the toolchain does or
+   it cannot see libc's errno at all.  */
